Z||000013||Fformula88||09-21-2001||11:47 AM||||I cannot argue the ability for a yellow or red Fiero to attract attention, but a cleaned and waxed White Fiero looks really good too!  I also think the black mouldings and mirrors and such on Fieros help set off the white.  I do not like white cars that are all white without any contrast.<P>I am somewhat biased to white, since thats the color of dads 85 SE (below) and it turns just as many heads as my bright red Formula!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000014||86seyellow||09-26-2001||10:13 AM||||I get lots of attetnition with this look. Black wing, black effects and leave the trim balck. Most yellows I have seen either have a yellow wing or have painted all the black trim. DOes anyone think I should take off the formulase stickers???<P>------------------<BR>I can go as fast as I want unless I get caught<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieropix1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Rick 88||09-26-2001||11:42 AM||||In my opinion the car would look cleaner without the Formula/SE emblems. However I think some small black Fiero "Pegasus" emblems would look sharp on your wheel centers.<P>Rick 88||||reg||7
